Add the missing DataSource.get_seq_length() to PushTDataSource.

rollout.py (and the sliced-dataset headroom filter) calls
data_source.get_seq_length(traj_idx), which the sibling DinoWorldModelDataSource
implements but PushTDataSource omits (the abstract base does not enforce it).
Without this, DINO-WM PushT long-rollout crashes with AttributeError. This mirrors
the sibling implementation exactly (self.seq_lengths is already populated).

--- a/src/wm_datasets/data_source/dino_wm/pusht.py
+++ b/src/wm_datasets/data_source/dino_wm/pusht.py
@@ -156,6 +156,9 @@
     def get_num_trajectories(self) -> int:
         return self.num_trajectories
 
+    def get_seq_length(self, index: int) -> int:
+        return int(self.seq_lengths[index].item())
+
     @property
     def action_dim(self) -> int:
         return self._action_dim
